  "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>American Empire</b> was a geopolitical text putting forth the notion that, due to the Flood, the United States has become an \"unintentional empire\" and must start behaving in a more mature fashion befitting of such a nation.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Overview\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Overview</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Part_1:_The_Origins_of_Empire\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\"><b>Part 1: The Origins of Empire</b></span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Part_2:_Reconciling_the_Empire_and_the_Republic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\"><b>Part 2: Reconciling the Empire and the Republic</b></span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Part_3:_The_Necessary_Doctrine\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\"><b>Part 3: The Necessary Doctrine</b></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Impact_on_US_foreign_policy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Impact on US foreign policy</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Overview\">Overview</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FAmerican_Empire%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D1&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_1:_The_Origins_of_Empire\"><b>Part 1: The Origins of Empire</b></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FAmerican_Empire%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D2&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The book was published while Stephen Michaels was president of the US Naval War College, and was a culmination of his ideas regarding US foreign policy and international relations.\n</p><p>Michaels began the book with an examination of what factors lead to America's economic power and geography's impact on a nation's foreign policy, focusing a great deal on how the country's rise to prominence after World War II. He identifies such features as geography, population, and government, and argues that American military supremacy is a consequence of these factors, reinforcing the belief in an \"Unintentional Empire.\"\n</p><p>The book goes on to describe the power vacuum left after the fall of the Soviet Union and what the period of conflicts in the Middle East reveal about America's political immaturity.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_2:_Reconciling_the_Empire_and_the_Republic\"><b>Part 2: Reconciling the Empire and the Republic</b></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FAmerican_Empire%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D3&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The book's second section outlines the risk that the Empire plays to the Republican experiment, though makes few political assertions. Michaels instead focuses on historical examples of Republicans that fell to Imperialism. He asserts that the risk for the US is not the slow surrender of legislative authority the the President but rather the rise of a Caesar in response to political discord and corruption at the Federal Level.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_3:_The_Necessary_Doctrine\"><b>Part 3: The Necessary Doctrine</b></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FAmerican_Empire%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D4&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The book's final chapter outwardly advocates for the next President to adopt a doctrine of local balance of power enabled by American military \"Viceroys\" who would command not only American troops, but have direct command over local forces; abandoning the alliance system of NATO in favor of more direct dominion. However, Michaels also argues that the US should reduce its permanent presence around the world in favor of a tiered system of priorities and deployments.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Tier 1: Diplomatic relations</li>\n<li>Tier 2: Pressuring regional powers</li>\n<li>Tier 3: Balance of power</li>\n<li>Tier 4: Military cooperation</li>\n<li>Tier 5: Direct Intervention</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Impact_on_US_foreign_policy\">Impact on US foreign policy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FAmerican_Empire%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D5&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261119081458\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.010 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 15/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.10_prod_secondrenaissance:pcache:idhash:2449-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20261119081458 and revision id 11202. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>",
